$ wavesleuth-devito --help

usage: wavesleuth-devito [-h] [--version]
                         {generate-world,simulate,invert,visualize-world,visualize-run,visualize-reconstruction,visualize-uncertainty,score,score-challenge,report,compare-acquisition,challenge,leaderboard,demo,active-demo,active-leaderboard,self-test,doctor,validate,challenge-suite,release-report}
                         ...

Scientific Battleship with Devito acoustic waves.

positional arguments:
  {generate-world,simulate,invert,visualize-world,visualize-run,visualize-reconstruction,visualize-uncertainty,score,score-challenge,report,compare-acquisition,challenge,leaderboard,demo,active-demo,active-leaderboard,self-test,doctor,validate,challenge-suite,release-report}
    generate-world      Generate a deterministic hidden world JSON file.
    simulate            Run Devito acoustic simulation for a world.
    invert              Invert observed traces with a simple search method.
    visualize-world     Plot a world velocity model.
    visualize-run       Plot receiver traces from a run.
    visualize-reconstruction
                        Plot reconstruction summary.
    visualize-uncertainty
                        Plot uncertainty/pseudo-probability from a
                        reconstruction mismatch map.
    score               Score a reconstruction against a true world.
    score-challenge     Score a challenge folder using its secret answer when
                        present.
    report              Generate a lightweight HTML experiment report.
    compare-acquisition
                        Compare acquisition presets on the same hidden world.
    challenge           Run a named budgeted challenge.
    leaderboard         Collect challenge_summary.json files into a sorted
                        leaderboard.
    demo                Run a complete tiny pipeline.
    active-demo         Run a multi-round active-sensing demo.
    active-leaderboard  Compare active-demo output directories.
    self-test           Run lightweight sanity checks.
    doctor              Print environment and package sanity checks.
    validate            Validate WaveSleuth artifacts and output directories.
    challenge-suite     Run the standard v0.9 challenge suite.
    release-report      Generate a compact HTML report for challenge/active
                        outputs.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
